From cp_set_bin_data_v3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: A22X CP_SET_BIN_DATA visibility consume + new
 VSC regs (v3)

Adds the webOS-style A22X HW binner visibility-stream consume sequence
behind FD2_USE_BIN_DATA=1.  Default behaviour is unchanged (Test 4
baseline: IGNORE_VISIBILITY, no per-tile consume) so this patch is
zero-risk to ship.

v3 changes (2026-05-12 from leia_perform_resolve decomp inspection):

  Previous v2 hung the GPU when FD2_USE_BIN_DATA=1 because the per-tile
  CP_WAIT_REG_EQ on RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE (bit 24) polled forever
  - the binner never latched the bit.

  Comparing to webOS leia_perform_resolve, the 12-dword block emitted
  between the binning IB return and the first per-tile consume looks
  exactly like:

    CP_SET_CONSTANT  A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL = 0
    OUT_PKT0         A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING (0xC00) = 0
    CP_EVENT_WRITE   CACHE_FLUSH (event 6)
    CP_WAIT_REG_EQ   RBBM_STATUS, val=0, mask=0x5f601000, poll=1

  Mesa v2 only emitted the first dword + a plain WFI.  Without the
  master 0xC00=0 disengage and the CACHE_FLUSH event, the binner's
  internal FIFOs never flush to memory, so RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE
  stays 0 and the per-tile poll hangs.  Mask 0x5f601000 on RBBM_STATUS
  covers VGT/SX/TPC/SC_CNTX/PA/RB_CNTX/SQ_CNTX0+17/VGT_NO_DMA - full
  3D pipeline idle, more thorough than CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE which only
  waits on the CP queue.

  v3 emits all four dwords behind a new env-var FD2_BIN_FULL_DISENGAGE
  (also implicitly enabled when FD2_USE_BIN_DATA=1, since the per-tile
  consume requires the full disengage to function).

Per-tile sequence from webOS leia_perform_resolve decomp:

  CP_WAIT_REG_EQ  reg=RBBM_DEBUG mask=0x01000000 val=0x01000000  poll=1
  CP_SET_BIN_DATA bin_data_addr=VSC_PIPE[p].DATA_ADDRESS
                  bin_size_addr=VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS + p*4

CP_WAIT_REG_EQ (opcode 0x52) and CP_SET_BIN_DATA (opcode 0x2f) are
both already in Mesa's adreno_pm4.xml for A2XX-A4XX.

Driver-side: new fd2_context::vsc_size_mem (0x1000-byte per-context BO
matching A3XX), allocated lazily in fd2_emit_tile_init next to
vsc_pipe_bo[].  Prelude writes A220_VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS pointed at it.
Per-tile renderprep emits WAIT_REG_EQ + SET_BIN_DATA for A22X when
FD2_USE_BIN_DATA is set; A20X keeps its working CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS
path.  patch_draws() picks USE_VISIBILITY when FD2_USE_BIN_DATA or
FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY is set on A22X.

XML-side (a2xx.xml):
  RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE @ bit 24
  A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING @ 0x0c00 (was raw 0xC00 in driver)
  A220_VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS      @ 0x0c02
  A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL    bitfields (BINNER_ENABLE0/1, LRZ_CLEAR_*)

Bisect plan (run on device, single build):

  default                       -> Test 4 baseline (no regression)
  FD2_BIN_FULL_DISENGAGE=1      -> v3 disengage alone (no per-tile change)
                                    if this still works at baseline rate,
                                    extra dwords are safe by themselves
  FD2_USE_BIN_DATA=1            -> v3 disengage + webOS per-tile consume
                                    if rates collapse to <12.5% cycle or
                                    1 hash, we have the right consume
                                    if hang again, the binner is still
                                    not actually producing visibility
                                    (root-cause deeper than 0098)
  FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY=1        -> control: known-bad A20X path

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/freedreno/registers/adreno/a2xx.xml
+++ b/src/freedreno/registers/adreno/a2xx.xml
@@ -1087,7 +1087,13 @@
 	<reg32 offset="0x0398" name="RBBM_PERFCOUNTER0_HI"/>
 	<reg32 offset="0x0399" name="RBBM_PERFCOUNTER1_LO"/>
 	<reg32 offset="0x039a" name="RBBM_PERFCOUNTER1_HI"/>
-	<reg32 offset="0x039b" name="RBBM_DEBUG"/>
+	<reg32 offset="0x039b" name="RBBM_DEBUG">
+		<!-- bit 24 is polled by the A220+ HW binner viz-consume sequence
+		     (CP_WAIT_REG_EQ in leia_perform_resolve): set when the binner has
+		     finished writing visibility data for the current pipe.  Verified
+		     against webOS libGLESv2 decomp 2026-05-12. -->
+		<bitfield name="A220_BINNER_DONE" pos="24" type="boolean"/>
+	</reg32>
 	<reg32 offset="0x039c" name="RBBM_PM_OVERRIDE1">
 		<bitfield name="RBBM_AHBCLK_PM_OVERRIDE" pos="0" type="boolean"/>
 		<bitfield name="SC_REG_SCLK_PM_OVERRIDE" pos="1" type="boolean"/>
@@ -1209,10 +1215,23 @@
 	<reg32 offset="0x0a44" name="MH_INTERRUPT_CLEAR"/>
 	<reg32 offset="0x0a54" name="MH_CLNT_INTF_CTRL_CONFIG1"/>
 	<reg32 offset="0x0a55" name="MH_CLNT_INTF_CTRL_CONFIG2"/>
+	<!-- A220 HW visibility-stream compressor (VSC) block @ 0x0c00.
+	     leia_configure_binning_pass (webOS libGLESv2 decomp) writes 1 here
+	     to engage the binner at the start of the binning pass. -->
+	<reg32 offset="0x0c00" name="A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING">
+		<bitfield name="ENABLE" pos="0" type="boolean"/>
+	</reg32>
 	<reg32 offset="0x0c01" name="A220_VSC_BIN_SIZE">
 		<bitfield name="WIDTH" low="0" high="4" shr="5" type="uint"/>
 		<bitfield name="HEIGHT" low="5" high="9" shr="5" type="uint"/>
 	</reg32>
+	<!-- Per-pipe visibility-stream length output base.  The binner writes one
+	     u32 per pipe (stride 4) to *(VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS + pipe*4); the per-tile
+	     CP_SET_BIN_DATA packet then loads that length so the visibility
+	     filter sees how many bytes of the pipe data BO are valid.
+	     Address documented from webOS leia_perform_resolve decomp; the exact
+	     register offset within 0x0c02..0x0c05 has not yet been narrowed. -->
+	<reg32 offset="0x0c02" name="A220_VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS"/>
 	<array offset="0x0c06" name="VSC_PIPE" stride="3" length="8">
 		<reg32 offset="0x0" name="CONFIG"/>
 		<reg32 offset="0x1" name="DATA_ADDRESS"/>
@@ -1499,7 +1518,16 @@
 	<reg32 offset="0x2208" name="RB_MODECONTROL">
 		<bitfield name="EDRAM_MODE" low="0" high="2" type="a2xx_rb_edram_mode"/>
 	</reg32>
-	<reg32 offset="0x2209" name="A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL"/>
+	<!-- A220 binner / LRZ control.  Empirical values observed in webOS:
+	     0x03 = engage HW binner (bits 0+1 set during binning pass setup)
+	     0x84 = LRZ clear mode (bits 2+7) during resolve-time clear
+	     0x00 = disengage / passthrough after binning IB completes -->
+	<reg32 offset="0x2209" name="A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL">
+		<bitfield name="BINNER_ENABLE0" pos="0" type="boolean"/>
+		<bitfield name="BINNER_ENABLE1" pos="1" type="boolean"/>
+		<bitfield name="LRZ_CLEAR_LO"   pos="2" type="boolean"/>
+		<bitfield name="LRZ_CLEAR_HI"   pos="7" type="boolean"/>
+	</reg32>
 	<reg32 offset="0x220a" name="RB_SAMPLE_POS"/>
 	<reg32 offset="0x220b" name="CLEAR_COLOR">
 		<bitfield name="RED" low="0" high="7"/>
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.c
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@
 static void
 fd2_context_destroy(struct pipe_context *pctx) in_dt
 {
+   struct fd2_context *fd2_ctx = fd2_context(fd_context(pctx));
+
+   if (fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem)
+      fd_bo_del(fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem);
+
    fd_context_destroy(pctx);
    free(pctx);
 }
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_context.h
@@ -18,6 +18,15 @@
     * vertices and tex coords:
     */
    struct pipe_resource *solid_vertexbuf;
+
+   /* A22X HW binner visibility-stream size BO.  The binner writes one
+    * u32 per pipe (8 pipes, 4 bytes each) to *(vsc_size_mem + pipe*4);
+    * the per-tile CP_SET_BIN_DATA packet then loads that length so the
+    * visibility filter sees how many bytes of the pipe data BO are
+    * valid for this tile's pipe.  Allocated lazily on first batch
+    * with use_hw_binning && is_a22x.
+    */
+   struct fd_bo *vsc_size_mem;
 };
 
 static inline struct fd2_context *
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -583,6 +583,7 @@
 fd2_emit_tile_init(struct fd_batch *batch) assert_dt
 {
    struct fd_context *ctx = batch->ctx;
+   struct fd2_context *fd2_ctx = fd2_context(ctx);
    struct fd_ringbuffer *ring = batch->gmem;
    struct pipe_framebuffer_state *pfb = &batch->framebuffer;
    const struct fd_gmem_stateobj *gmem = batch->gmem_state;
@@ -747,12 +748,21 @@
     *   FD2_SKIP_BINNING_IB    skip fd2_emit_ib(batch->binning)
     *   FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY   re-enable patch_draws(USE_VIS) + per-tile
     *                          CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS for A22X (WILL HANG)
+    *   FD2_USE_BIN_DATA       enable webOS-style per-tile consume
+    *                          (CP_WAIT_REG_EQ RBBM_DEBUG bit24 +
+    *                          CP_SET_BIN_DATA) — implies FULL_DISENGAGE
+    *   FD2_BIN_FULL_DISENGAGE add 0xC00=0 + CACHE_FLUSH event +
+    *                          CP_WAIT_REG_EQ RBBM_STATUS to the
+    *                          disengage block (v3 — without these
+    *                          webOS-equivalent dwords the binner's
+    *                          RBBM_DEBUG bit24 never gets latched and
+    *                          the per-tile poll hangs forever)
     *   FD2_VSC_DUMP           dump VSC pipe BO contents per batch (diag)
     */
-   /* Always allocate VSC pipe BOs for A22X if use_hw_binning is active —
-    * per-tile renderprep emits CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS referencing
-    * ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[tile->p], so the BOs must exist regardless of
-    * whether the prelude runs.
+   /* Always allocate VSC pipe BOs + the per-context VSC_SIZE BO for A22X
+    * when use_hw_binning is active — per-tile renderprep emits
+    * CP_SET_BIN_DATA referencing both, so they must exist regardless of
+    * whether the prelude actually runs (FD2_SKIP_PRELUDE can disable it).
     */
    if (is_a22x(ctx->screen) && use_hw_binning(batch)) {
       for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
@@ -762,6 +772,14 @@
             assert(ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[i]);
          }
       }
+      if (!fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem) {
+         /* 32 bytes is enough (8 pipes × 4 bytes), but match the A3XX
+          * 0x1000 page allocation so the BO lands on its own page and
+          * can never share a cache line with unrelated state. */
+         fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem =
+            fd_bo_new(ctx->dev, 0x1000, 0, "a22x_vsc_size");
+         assert(fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem);
+      }
    }
 
    if (is_a22x(ctx->screen) && !getenv("FD2_SKIP_PRELUDE")) {
@@ -847,6 +865,16 @@
          OUT_RING(ring, fd_bo_size(ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[i]));
       }
 
+      /* VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS: tell the binner where to write the per-pipe
+       * visibility-stream length (one u32 per pipe).  Mirrors A3XX
+       * update_vsc_pipe(), but using OUT_PKT0 because A2XX VSC regs
+       * are below 0x2000 (CP_SET_CONSTANT range).  The per-tile
+       * CP_SET_BIN_DATA packet later loads from this BO at offset
+       * tile->p * 4 to feed the visibility filter.
+       */
+      OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_A220_VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS, 1);
+      OUT_RELOC(ring, fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem, 0, 0, 0);
+
       /* Explicit disengage of any previously-engaged binner before
        * re-engaging in this batch.
        *
@@ -867,12 +895,13 @@
       OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
       OUT_WFI(ring);
 
-      /* A220_VSC_ENABLE @ 0xC00 = 1 -- undocumented master enable.
-       * webOS writes this via a type-0 PM4 packet. The register is not
-       * in a2xx.xml so we use the raw address.
+      /* A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING.ENABLE = 1 -- master engage for the
+       * HW binner.  webOS writes this via a type-0 PM4 packet at the
+       * start of leia_configure_binning_pass; without it the binner does
+       * not advance past stream-out setup.
        */
-      OUT_PKT0(ring, 0xC00, 1);
-      OUT_RING(ring, 1);
+      OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING_ENABLE);
 
       /* Engage the binner: A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL = 3 (webOS value).
        * WFI follows immediately after, per webOS ordering — earlier v2
@@ -919,21 +948,26 @@
    }
 
    if (use_hw_binning(batch)) {
-      /* A22X: default to IGNORE_VISIBILITY because the visibility filter
-       * (patch_draws(USE_VISIBILITY) + per-tile CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS)
-       * hard-hangs the GPU on A22X — confirmed across multiple bisect
-       * tests including with the binning IB actually running.
-       *
-       * webOS likely uses a different A22X-specific visibility-consume
-       * packet. Until that's identified, ship the working "binning IB
-       * runs, no visibility filter" config (Test 4) as the default.
+      /* A22X default = IGNORE_VISIBILITY (Test 4 shipping baseline).
+       * Two diagnostic env-vars switch the A22X consume path:
+       *
+       *   FD2_USE_BIN_DATA       webOS-style CP_SET_BIN_DATA per tile +
+       *                          CP_WAIT_REG_EQ on RBBM_DEBUG.BINNER_DONE.
+       *                          Requires USE_VISIBILITY so draws consult
+       *                          the stream the packet just bound.
+       *   FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY   legacy A20X CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS path.
+       *                          Confirmed to hard-hang on A22X — kept
+       *                          only as a falsifier knob.
        *
-       * Set FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY=1 to revert to USE_VISIBILITY (will hang
-       * on A22X — diagnostic only). A20X keeps its working filter. */
+       * A20X always uses USE_VISIBILITY (its CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS path
+       * is the original, working freedreno binning consume).
+       */
+      bool a22x = is_a22x(ctx->screen);
+      bool a22x_visibility = a22x && (getenv("FD2_USE_BIN_DATA") ||
+                                      getenv("FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY"));
       patch_draws(batch,
-                  (is_a22x(ctx->screen) && !getenv("FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY"))
-                     ? IGNORE_VISIBILITY
-                     : USE_VISIBILITY);
+                  (!a22x || a22x_visibility) ? USE_VISIBILITY
+                                             : IGNORE_VISIBILITY);
 
       if (is_a20x(ctx->screen)) {
          /* A20X hw binning: shader-memexport mechanism.
@@ -1062,11 +1096,52 @@
           * Subsequent per-tile rendering uses the visibility data the
           * binner wrote to VSC_PIPE BOs, but the binner itself should
           * not be re-engaged for render-pass draws.
+          *
+          * webOS-equivalent block (leia_perform_resolve decomp, 12 dwords
+          * gated on `binner_used`):
+          *   1. LRZ_VSC_CONTROL = 0                  (disengage binner)
+          *   2. A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING (0xC00)=0 (master disengage)
+          *   3. CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH (event 6) (flush binner FIFOs;
+          *                                            sets RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE)
+          *   4. CP_WAIT_REG_EQ RBBM_STATUS, mask=0x5f601000  (3D pipe idle)
+          *
+          * v2 of this patch only emitted (1) + WFI; per-tile
+          * CP_WAIT_REG_EQ then polled RBBM_DEBUG bit 24 forever because
+          * the CACHE_FLUSH event was missing.  v3 adds (2), (3), (4) to
+          * mirror webOS exactly.
+          *
+          * Default-disabled via FD2_BIN_FULL_DISENGAGE so the v2 path
+          * remains the fallback if v3 still doesn't unblock the bit.
           */
          OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
          OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL));
          OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
-         OUT_WFI(ring);
+
+         if (getenv("FD2_BIN_FULL_DISENGAGE") || getenv("FD2_USE_BIN_DATA")) {
+            /* (2) Master disengage of the A220 binner module. */
+            OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_A220_VSC_PIPE_PARTITIONING, 1);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0);
+
+            /* (3) CACHE_FLUSH event — flushes binner internal FIFOs and
+             *     latches RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE (bit 24).
+             */
+            OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+            OUT_RING(ring, CACHE_FLUSH);
+
+            /* (4) Explicit poll for full 3D pipeline idle.  webOS uses
+             *     this in place of WFI; the mask covers VGT/SX/TPC/SC/PA/
+             *     RB/SQ_CNTX0+17/VGT_NO_DMA — every stage that could
+             *     still be holding binner state.  WFI alone only waits
+             *     on the CP queue and is not sufficient here.
+             */
+            OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_REG_EQ, 4);
+            OUT_RING(ring, REG_A2XX_RBBM_STATUS);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x5f601000);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000001);
+         } else {
+            OUT_WFI(ring);
+         }
 
          /* DIAGNOSTIC: marker 6 = disengage complete */
          OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_AXXX_CP_SCRATCH_REG5, 1);
@@ -1163,11 +1238,44 @@
       OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MAX));
       OUT_RING(ring, tile->n);
 
-      /* TODO only emit this when tile->p changes */
-      /* A22X: default skip the per-tile CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS that
-       * points the rasterizer at the VSC pipe BO — hangs the GPU on
-       * A22X. A20X keeps its working filter. See patch_draws() above. */
-      if (!is_a22x(ctx->screen) || getenv("FD2_FORCE_VISIBILITY")) {
+      if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
+         /* A22X visibility-stream consume.  Matches webOS
+          * leia_perform_resolve per-tile sequence:
+          *
+          *   CP_WAIT_REG_EQ  reg=RBBM_DEBUG mask=0x01000000 val=0x01000000
+          *   CP_SET_BIN_DATA pipe_data_addr=VSC_PIPE[p].DATA_ADDRESS
+          *                   bin_size_addr =VSC_SIZE_ADDRESS + p*4
+          *
+          * The WAIT_REG_EQ stalls the CP until the binner reports its
+          * per-pipe stream is complete (RBBM_DEBUG.A220_BINNER_DONE).
+          * Then CP_SET_BIN_DATA tells the visibility filter where to
+          * find the stream + how many bytes are valid for this tile's
+          * pipe.  Mesa's CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS path (used on A20X) is
+          * the wrong consume packet for A22X and hangs the GPU.
+          *
+          * Default-disabled: needs FD2_USE_BIN_DATA=1 in the
+          * environment so we can bisect against the Test 4 baseline
+          * (IGNORE_VISIBILITY, no per-tile consume) without rebuild.
+          */
+         if (getenv("FD2_USE_BIN_DATA")) {
+            /* CP_WAIT_REG_EQ packet, 4 dwords:
+             *   reg, value, mask, wait_count (poll-interval)
+             */
+            OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_REG_EQ, 4);
+            OUT_RING(ring, REG_A2XX_RBBM_DEBUG);
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x01000000);     /* A220_BINNER_DONE = 1 */
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x01000000);     /* mask */
+            OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000001);     /* poll interval */
+
+            OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_BIN_DATA, 2);
+            OUT_RELOC(ring, pipe_bo, 0, 0, 0);       /* BIN_DATA_ADDR */
+            OUT_RELOC(ring, fd2_ctx->vsc_size_mem,   /* BIN_SIZE_ADDR */
+                      tile->p * 4, 0, 0);
+         }
+      } else {
+         /* A20X path: CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS points the rasterizer at
+          * the VSC pipe BO.  Confirmed working for A20X.
+          */
          OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS, 1);
          OUT_RELOC(ring, pipe_bo, 0, 0, 0);
       }
